foundation.com.au/downloads/hypertension_management_guide_2004.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>The National Heart Foundation of Australia and Cardiac Society of Australian and New Zealand</collab></person-group><article-title>Reducing Risk in Heart Disease 2007: Guidelines for preventing cardiovascular events in people with coronary heart disease</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.heartfoundation.com.au/downloads/ReducingRisk_HeartDisease_FullGuide_2007.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Centre for General Practice Integration Studies</collab></person-group><source>Reviewing the contribution of general practice to a well-functioning and comprehensive primary health care system</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Sydney , University of New South Wales</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cronbach</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Coefficient alpha and the internal structure of tests</article-title><source>Psychometrika</source><year>1951</year><fpage>297</fpage><lpage>334</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF02310555</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spector</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name></person-group><source>Summated rating scale construction: an introduction</source><year>1992</year><publisher-name>Sage publications: California</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marsh</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name><name><surname>Ball</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interjudgemental reliability of review for the Journal of Educational Psychology</article-title><source>Journal of Educational Psychology</source><year>1981</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>872</fpage><lpage>880</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0022-0663.73.6.872</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>SPSS Inc.</collab></person-group><source>SPSS Base 12.0.1 for Windows</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Chicago , SPSS</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nunnally</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><source>Psychometric Theory</source><year>1978</year><edition>2nd ed</edition><publisher-name>New York , McGraw Hill</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Splaine</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Batalden</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Building measurement and data collection into medical practice.</article-title><source>Annals Int Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>128</volume><fpage>460</fpage><lpage>466</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grol</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Leatherman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improving quality in British primary care: seeking the right balance</article-title><source>Br J Gen Prac</source><year>2002</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>S3</fpage><lpage>S4</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Department of Health UK</collab></person-group><source>Quality and Outcomes Framework</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>London  </publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khanna</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Missing medical information adversely affects care of patients</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2005</year><volume>330</volume><fpage>276</fpage><lpage>a-</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.330.7486.276-a</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Yeazel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Center</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Validity of residents' self-reported cardiovascular disease prevention activities: the Preventive Medicine Attitudes and Activities Questionnaire</article-title><source>Preventive Medicine</source><year>2002</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>241</fpage><lpage>248</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10964638</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/pmed.2000.0705</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynolds</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Empathy and quality of care</article-title><source>BrJ Gen Prac</source><year>2002</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>S9</fpage><lpage>S13</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>